  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThe western upper ridge will remain fairly flat with a WNW flow\naloft through midweek with a series of weak shortwaves pushing\nalong the international border. This will keep temperatures\nslightly below normal. One wave passes through this morning with\nisolated showers mainly south of Fort Peck Lake. Another wave\nmoves through this afternoon and evening with scattered showers\nand thunderstorms. Additions waves are expected for Monday night\nand again Tuesday afternoon and night. \n\nUpper ridge builds into the area for Wednesday, Thursday and \nFriday with a return to warmer and drier conditions for the end of\nthe week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nMain deviations to the NBM were to spread pops across a larger\narea for Sunday night through Monday night. Confidence is moderate\nin timing the various waves the next few days.",
